10
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:28,030
Hell yeah.

11
00:00:28,890 --> 00:00:29,650
Sure do.

12
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:32,180
Yeah, I sure do.

13
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:34,400
I love Christmas morning even as an adult.

14
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:39,140
Especially I think because of the special breakfast you get like pancakes, scrambled eggs.

15
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:49,060
But anyways, we're going to be taking a look at a situation here where a kid is opening Christmas presents and we're preparing a meal for Christmas because that day people are going to come over.

16
00:00:49,520 --> 00:01:06,560
So let's listen to this dialogue for the first time.

17
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:26,800
Dad, dad, dad, wake up.

18
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:27,140
It's Christmas.

19
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:30,450
Timmy, it's too early for this.

20
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:33,500
Look, it's six in the morning.

21
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:34,840
Go back to bed.

22
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:35,740
No way.

23
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,280
Santa already came and left all our presents.

24
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:41,820
Can we go open them, please, please?

25
00:01:43,070 --> 00:01:44,550
Of course we can, honey.

26
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:47,400
Bill, come on, get dressed.

27
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:48,400
Fine.

28
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:50,250
Not like Santa brought me any gifts.

29
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:53,610
Bill, honestly, you can be such a grouch sometimes.

30
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:02,220
Look at all these presents under the Christmas tree.

31
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:03,000
Awesome.

32
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,660
All right, Timmy, knock yourself out.

33
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:09,480
We should get ready and head to the market to buy everything for Christmas dinner tonight.

34
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:10,560
Yeah, you're right.

35
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:14,900
It's the first time we're hosting Christmas dinner at our house, so everything has to be perfect.

36
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:16,960
I got the list right here.

37
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:23,300
Ham, turkey, mashed potatoes, ingredients for the gravy, and of course, yams.

38
00:02:23,980 --> 00:02:26,480
My dad offered to bring the eggnog, so we should be set.

39
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,680
All right, we're back.

40
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:37,650
So there were a couple of different and interesting words there, so let's take a look at them now in Language Takeaway.

41
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:41,120
Language Takeaway.

42
00:02:41,610 --> 00:02:45,710
Okay, this first word is not a very happy word.

43
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:56,160
It's a word that we try not to use too much around the Christmas season, but sometimes you're just tired of people because the holidays is all about people and doing stuff.

44
00:02:56,160 --> 00:03:00,280
Someone who is not being very happy, someone who's a little bit grumpy is called a grouch.

45
00:03:00,390 --> 00:03:04,810
Okay, so a person that's not very happy, not very friendly is a grouch.

46
00:03:06,270 --> 00:03:08,050
I don't want to open presents.

47
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,270
This is stupid.

48
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:12,400
Okay, that's a grouch.

49
00:03:12,750 --> 00:03:17,390
Okay, so a person is a grouch, or you can act like a grouch, or be a grouch.

50
00:03:17,410 --> 00:03:18,310
Don't be a grouch!

51
00:03:18,410 --> 00:03:18,790
All right.

52
00:03:19,570 --> 00:03:26,010
And, well, they were talking about heading to the market to buy something for dinner, so to head to.

53
00:03:26,250 --> 00:03:31,390
Okay, to head to is a way to say to go towards some place or to go somewhere.

54
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:37,400
All right, so if I'm driving my car and you ask me where I'm going, I'm saying, oh, I'm heading to the bank.

55
00:03:37,530 --> 00:03:42,010
Right, so to head to means to be on your way somewhere, I'm going somewhere.

56
00:03:43,030 --> 00:03:45,850
It's a way to say that you're in the process of going.

57
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:50,520
You can't say, next year I will head to Alaska.

58
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:51,800
It doesn't make as much sense.

59
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:56,920
You usually say, I'm heading to the bank, or let's head to the market.

60
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:05,680
And well, they were talking about heading to the market because they are hosting Christmas dinner, so to host.

61
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:08,810
To host is a very important holiday term.

62
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:17,430
It's a verb, you do it, and it means that you are the person who has the special dinner and your friends and family, they come to your house.

63
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:22,490
Okay, so we could say, this Christmas, I'm hosting the dinner at my house.

64
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:25,400
So, I want everyone to come to my house and eat.

65
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:27,410
All right, and it can also be a noun, right?

66
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:29,280
You can say, I am a host.

67
00:04:29,630 --> 00:04:29,870
Exactly.

68
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:31,280
I'm the host of this dinner.

69
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:33,440
Right, and it doesn't have to be holidays either.

70
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:36,180
You could say, hey, Marco, how about you host a dinner next week?

71
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:36,680
I'll come.

72
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:38,320
Right, okay.

73
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:39,320
I'll bring wine.

74
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:44,440
All right, so to host a dinner or to host a party, etc.

75
00:04:44,440 --> 00:04:51,280
And our fourth word for language takeaway is probably the most popular drink during the Christmas season, eggnog.

76
00:04:51,570 --> 00:04:53,610
Okay, it sounds kind of disgusting.

77
00:04:53,990 --> 00:04:55,630
Yeah, a drink with egg.

78
00:04:56,130 --> 00:05:00,050
But it's a very popular creamy eggy drink.

79
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:03,640
It's very thick and it's cream colored.

80
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:05,330
And normally, you add a little bit of rum.

81
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:08,440
Okay, so it's alcoholic.

82
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:17,320
And you drink it warm and it's kind of just a thick, warm alcoholic beverage that's very very popular and my dad loves it.

83
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:18,000
During Christmas, right?

84
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:18,740
During Christmas.

85
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:20,960
You don't have it like any other day.

86
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:22,020
No, you wouldn't want to.

87
00:05:22,140 --> 00:05:22,700
It's too heavy.

88
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:27,040
But it's very very popular like the days before Christmas and on Christmas.

89
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:28,280
Okay, so eggnog.

90
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:29,260
Very good.

